	(text "Things MMU Needs to do:\n-----------------------\n-Reset: after reset MMU should allow CPU to access vector area in ROM and initialize MMU.\n-On an interrupt of SWI OS may need access to USER stack. First to save but also for contents.\n-Switch to OS/Supervisor mode in case of SWI, interrupts, NMI.\n-Sequence to switch back to user mode.\n\nUser Process:\n-------------\n0x0000-0xMFFF	Data page (Can be set to be 1-8 8k pages)\n0xN000-0xOFFF	Far Data Page0 (1 optional 8k page, always follows data page)\n0xP000-0xQFFF	Far Data Page1 (1 optional 8k page, always follows data page)\n0x?000-0x?FFF	Code Page (0-7 8k pages)\n0xC000-0xDFFF	Far Code Page (1 optional 8k page, always before OS page)\n0xE000-0xEFFF	User area, same page as OS area. User writable.\n0xF000-0xFFFF	OS Area\n\nVectors:\n--------\nFFFE	~{RESET}\nFFFC	~{NMI}\nFFFA	SWI\nFFF8	~{IRQ1}\nFFF6	~{IRQ2} Input Capture\nFFF4	~{IRQ2} Output Compare\nFFF3	~{IRQ2} Timer Overflow\nFFF0	~{IRQ2} SCI\n\nIRQ1 Sources:\n-------------\nMC6840, MC6844(?), MC6850, MC6821, SPI, RTC, expansion bus (Floppy, DSP, video, KB, Mouse, GPIB...)\nShould/Can the MC6821 be used as interrupt controller?\n"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 237.49 -611.632 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Monaco")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "10477282-2799-4eaa-bb2e-3cb7e77c134c")
	)
	(text "Componenets to add:\n-------------------\nFloppy controller.\nFPU.\n\nTo do:\n------\nMemory map, address decoding.\nSPI\nMMDS like debug/trace.\nDMA cycles when E is low? A14-A21 generation during DMA.\nSlow peripheral bus (RTC).\nMode entry following reset."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 49.53 -598.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e55c936d-a760-44f2-bb93-552bc72969ba")
	)
	(text "Swtich to Supervisor mode:\n--------------------------\n1-Fetch byte in the vector area && A15 == 0;\n    => State = 1;\n    else State = 0;\n2-Immediatelly fetch byte in the vector area + 1 && State == 1;\n    => State = 2;\n    else State = 0;\n3-Immediately fetch opcode in designated OS range && State == 2;\n    => Mode = Supervisor;\n    State = 0;\n\nWhat to do if an NMI is triggered while in the vector fetch sequence?\n\nOS Range (within last 4K of memory) will contain OS entry points for interrupts and\nother things. Potentially some OS data. Not user writable.\nWhen entering OS, the data is in the USER stack, SP was not changed.\n\nStack Monitor:\n--------------\nOS can determine a location that if writen will cause stack overflow NMI.\nMust leave space in the stack for NMI entry and exit.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 134.874 -598.17 0)
